glamor: enable DRI3 only when dma-bufs can be imported and exported.

DRI3 passes buffers as dma-bufs. A PixmapFromBuffer request (and a PRIME
import) reaches gbm_bo_import(GBM_BO_IMPORT_FD), which calls the DRI
driver's createImageFromFds. Mesa 21.3.9 on illumos builds its Gallium
drivers without dma-buf import (PIPE_CAP_DMABUF is 1 only on Linux and the
BSDs), so the function pointer is NULL, and GBM calls it without checking:
one DRI3 client request made Xorg with glamor on virtio-gpu die with
SIGSEGV at address 0 in glamor_back_pixmap_from_fd(). Kernel drivers
without PRIME (the legacy gfx-drm i915) cannot pass dma-bufs at all.

Turn DRI3 on only when the kernel reports PRIME import and export and EGL
offers EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import, which Mesa sets exactly when the
driver's import exists. Otherwise GLX clients use DRI2, as before.

The same checks are missing upstream (21.1 reaches GBM_BO_IMPORT_FD
unconditionally); the crash itself is Mesa's (GBM should fail with ENOSYS).

--- a/glamor/glamor_egl.c
+++ b/glamor/glamor_egl.c
@@ -846,10 +846,32 @@
      */
     lastGLContext = NULL;
 #ifdef GLAMOR_HAS_GBM
+    /*
+     * DRI3 passes buffers as dma-bufs: PixmapFromBuffer (and a PRIME
+     * import) goes through gbm_bo_import(GBM_BO_IMPORT_FD), BufferFromPixmap
+     * through gbm_bo_get_fd(). That needs PRIME import and export in the
+     * kernel and the DRI driver's dma-buf import, which Mesa advertises as
+     * EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import. Mesa 21.3's GBM calls a missing import
+     * function anyway, and the server crashes.
+     */
     if (epoxy_has_egl_extension(glamor_egl->display,
                                 "EGL_KHR_gl_texture_2D_image") &&
-        epoxy_has_gl_extension("GL_OES_EGL_image"))
-        glamor_egl->dri3_capable = TRUE;
+        epoxy_has_gl_extension("GL_OES_EGL_image")) {
+        uint64_t prime = 0;
+
+        if (drmGetCap(glamor_egl->fd, DRM_CAP_PRIME, &prime) != 0 ||
+            !(prime & DRM_PRIME_CAP_IMPORT) || !(prime & DRM_PRIME_CAP_EXPORT))
+            xf86DrvMsg(scrn->scrnIndex, X_INFO,
+                       "glamor: DRI3 disabled: the kernel driver lacks "
+                       "PRIME import or export\n");
+        else if (!epoxy_has_egl_extension(glamor_egl->display,
+                                          "EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import"))
+            xf86DrvMsg(scrn->scrnIndex, X_INFO,
+                       "glamor: DRI3 disabled: the EGL driver cannot "
+                       "import dma-bufs (no EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import)\n");
+        else
+            glamor_egl->dri3_capable = TRUE;
+    }
 #endif
 
     glamor_egl->saved_free_screen = scrn->FreeScreen;
